(5049674, 735871, 83313, '<td valign="top">3 things...<br/> <br/>A) Lots of compression. Your file size of only 53k killed a lot of the detail in this scene with compression. Use as little compression as you can get away with and still stay within challenge limits.<br/> <br/>B) White balance looks weird. I know this is probably late in the day, but the yellowish cast still looks odd to me.<br/> <br/>C) <strike>I can''t stretch my definition of a mirror to include a reflection in water.</strike> <br/> <br/>Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back.<br/> <br/>Also added: (4) I now see a vignette on the image, which is not allowed in basic editing, unless it was created in-camera. Your entry may end up getting disqualified for that element.</td>', '3 things... A) Lots of compression. Your file size of only 53k killed a lot of the detail in this scene with compression. Use as little compression as you can get away with and still stay within challenge limits. B) White balance looks weird. I know this is probably late in the day, but the yellowish cast still looks odd to me. C) I can''t stretch my definition of a mirror to include a reflection in water.  Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back. Also added: (4) I now see a vignette on the image, which is not allowed in basic editing, unless it was created in-camera. Your entry may end up getting disqualified for that element.', '2008-11-06 21:41:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5049677, 736531, 83313, '<td valign="top"><strike>Not sure that this reflection really counts as mirror to me</strike>. Nice shot of this bird, however.<br/> <br/>Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and possibly give you some points back.</td>', 'Not sure that this reflection really counts as mirror to me. Nice shot of this bird, however. Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and possibly give you some points back.', '2008-11-06 21:42:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5049678, 736606, 83313, '<td valign="top">A very cool shot, and <strike>I am really having to try and stretch my definition of a mirror to give this the high vote it ought to get</strike>. I''m afraid I have to give it a somewhat lower vote for now, though I may re-evaluate my thinking later on.<br/> <br/>Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back.</td>', 'A very cool shot, and I am really having to try and stretch my definition of a mirror to give this the high vote it ought to get. I''m afraid I have to give it a somewhat lower vote for now, though I may re-evaluate my thinking later on. Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back.', '2008-11-06 21:42:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5049718, 736285, 83313, '<td valign="top">I really, <b>really</b> like this. However, I can''t stretch my definition of a mirror to include a reflection in a water. This would have done well in the <br/>"Reflections without mirrors" challenge. This shot gets a rare combination, a 4 and a fave.<br/> <br/>Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it''s only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back.</td>', 'I really, really like this. However, I can''t stretch my definition of a mirror to include a reflection in a water. This would have done well in the "Reflections without mirrors" challenge. This shot gets a rare combination, a 4 and a fave. Added: After reading the discussions in the score thread, I went and looked up definitions of "mirror" from several sources. I did not consider a reflection in water to be a mirror. Several sources use that as a secondary definition, so I must now consider a reflection in water to be a creative interpretation. I think it''s only fair to reevaluate my original vote on this and give you some points back.', '2008-11-06 22:07:04.000000', NULL, 1),
