(5058556, 736510, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>nicely seen, out of the box approach<br/> <br/></td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee!nicely seen, out of the box approach ', '2008-11-12 01:08:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058558, 735808, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/> <br/>bright, beautiful, dynamic, intriguing</td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee! bright, beautiful, dynamic, intriguing', '2008-11-12 01:08:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058560, 735930, 83313, '<td valign="top">I see I was on target about a few things. Even though I was one who didn''t care for it, I applaud you for entering the one you liked, In spite of the flak and low voting you expected and got. Sometimes you just don''t know how it will be received. You have to throw it against the wall, and if it sticks then it''s art!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-12 01:10:53.</i></td>', 'I see I was on target about a few things. Even though I was one who didn''t care for it, I applaud you for entering the one you liked, In spite of the flak and low voting you expected and got. Sometimes you just don''t know how it will be received. You have to throw it against the wall, and if it sticks then it''s art!', '2008-11-12 01:09:19.000000', '2008-11-12 01:10:53.000000', 0),
(5058561, 736713, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677020" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award WINNER!<br/>more than just a run-of-the-mill pet shot--good composition (I think the having the eyes in the reflection would have thrown this off) and wonderful tonality</td>', 'PostLuminous Award WINNER!more than just a run-of-the-mill pet shot--good composition (I think the having the eyes in the reflection would have thrown this off) and wonderful tonality', '2008-11-12 01:10:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058574, 735719, 83313, '<td valign="top">I found this entry particularly interesting, as it is a similar reflection-in-a-building concept as my own entry in this challenge. Looking forward to seeing what you turn out in the future.</td>', 'I found this entry particularly interesting, as it is a similar reflection-in-a-building concept as my own entry in this challenge. Looking forward to seeing what you turn out in the future.', '2008-11-12 01:16:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058588, 736665, 83313, '<td valign="top">Per your request a couple of tips:<br/> <br/>-I think your A520 has some manual controls, including aperture priority. For a shot like this in low light use a low ISO on a tripod, to allow for a slow shutter speed without camera shake.<br/> <br/>-Some basic image adjustments will help as well. I would suggest the most basic as being levels, curves, saturation and sharpening. Levels is the first and most important, IMO. <br/> <br/>-On the compression thing. Most photo editors will have the compression settings in the file save dialog somewhere. If you need a good and free photo editor, with many of the features of the big names, I like to recommend <a href="https://www.getpaint.net" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">paint.net</a> <br/> <br/>-The shot itself just does not have much to it. I would describe it as deadpan. Maybe a tilt, or something colorful reflected in the mirror?<br/> <br/>Oh, and congrats on your first ribbon, even if it''s the brown. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=728734" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">I''ve got one as well.</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-12 09:33:45.</i></td>', 'Per your request a couple of tips: -I think your A520 has some manual controls, including aperture priority. For a shot like this in low light use a low ISO on a tripod, to allow for a slow shutter speed without camera shake. -Some basic image adjustments will help as well. I would suggest the most basic as being levels, curves, saturation and sharpening. Levels is the first and most important, IMO.  -On the compression thing. Most photo editors will have the compression settings in the file save dialog somewhere. If you need a good and free photo editor, with many of the features of the big names, I like to recommend paint.net  -The shot itself just does not have much to it. I would describe it as deadpan. Maybe a tilt, or something colorful reflected in the mirror? Oh, and congrats on your first ribbon, even if it''s the brown. I''ve got one as well.', '2008-11-12 01:27:42.000000', '2008-11-12 09:33:45.000000', 0),
(5058589, 735085, 92546, '<td valign="top">awesome work Ben!</td>', 'awesome work Ben!', '2008-11-12 01:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058591, 736713, 68504, '<td valign="top">Beautiful expression, and wonderful filling the frame. Very fine.</td>', 'Beautiful expression, and wonderful filling the frame. Very fine.', '2008-11-12 01:30:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058592, 736530, 54645, '<td valign="top">Ah, I knew this was your photograph! Always so simple and elegant. My question, Irene, is what is going on at the bottom of the photograph. It looks like a ring of flare (green on my monitor), I''m sure it is a reflection from the mirror. No one mentioned it so it may have gone largely unnoticed. Nicely done as always.</td>', 'Ah, I knew this was your photograph! Always so simple and elegant. My question, Irene, is what is going on at the bottom of the photograph. It looks like a ring of flare (green on my monitor), I''m sure it is a reflection from the mirror. No one mentioned it so it may have gone largely unnoticed. Nicely done as always.', '2008-11-12 01:31:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058604, 736678, 40718, '<td valign="top">You don''t need my help in the Olympics... ;)</td>', 'You don''t need my help in the Olympics... ;)', '2008-11-12 01:41:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5058646, 736705, 31776, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=20324" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">artvet</a>Very underscored IMO! Well executed! Probably people didn''t like the softens.<br/> <br/>Thanks Arter, <br/> <br/>I did play around with the image after the challenge began and found a couple of areas I could have improved on especially sharpness. <br/> <br/>I was hoping to score a little higher with this but realised I would lose some votes due to not having a real mirror in the image, picky picky! To be honest though I did consider putting a small mirror in the foreground but had problems with composing the image the way I wanted, it just spoiled the overall effect.  <br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for their votes and comments<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-12 02:10:47.</i></td>', ' artvetVery underscored IMO! Well executed! Probably people didn''t like the softens. Thanks Arter,  I did play around with the image after the challenge began and found a couple of areas I could have improved on especially sharpness.  I was hoping to score a little higher with this but realised I would lose some votes due to not having a real mirror in the image, picky picky! To be honest though I did consider putting a small mirror in the foreground but had problems with composing the image the way I wanted, it just spoiled the overall effect.   Thanks everyone for their votes and comments', '2008-11-12 02:09:13.000000', '2008-11-12 02:10:47.000000', 0),
